1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,985
Neoh has booked a tennis court.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,460
His friend agreed off-app, then cancelled.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:10,685
They never joined a session or committed any funds.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,835
Now Neoh needs players, and a firmer commitment.

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:21,260
New to Booking Web Manager, Neoh starts at the landing page.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,610
The animated court catches his eye, and he explores the sports
on offer.

7
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:33,010
The page explains how to find games, check details, and share a
court.

8
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:37,710
He already has a venue. Now he needs people to play with.

9
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:45,660
Neoh creates his first public tennis session for Sunday, six to
eight.

10
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:52,285
He enters Kallang Tennis Hub and the thirty-dollar venue cost.

11
00:00:55,300 --> 00:01:00,260
Three places include Neoh. Each guest contributes ten dollars.

12
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:04,485
He saves the session. Now two places are open.

13
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:09,760
Meet Harrison. He wants a game that fits his weekend.

14
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:14,635
Harrison uses a prepared demo account with a funded wallet.

15
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:20,210
Harrison narrows Discover to tennis in the Central region.

16
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:26,735
Neoh's Sunday session gives him the venue, time and price up
front.

17
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,810
He reviews the booking before choosing to join.

18
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,310
The confirmation explains that ten dollars will be held from his
wallet.

19
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,735
He confirms, and his place is secured.

20
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,910
Harrison can see both his place and his contribution, without
chasing a chat.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,260
In Wallet, his available balance falls from twenty dollars to
ten.

22
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:03,360
The other ten dollars is held for this session.

23
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:06,585
It has not been paid to Neoh yet.

24
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:12,285
Joseph discovers the same public session from his own account.

25
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:20,910
He checks the details and confirms his ten-dollar share too.

26
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:31,910
Back in Neoh's Booking Room, all three places are now accounted
for.

27
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:40,710
Neoh, Harrison and Joseph can rotate through their tennis
practice.

28
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,085
The court no longer goes to waste.

29
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:49,835
And the participant list gives Neoh one clear view of who is
playing.

30
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:56,585
But what happens if somebody's plans change again?

31
00:02:56,750 --> 00:03:02,535
These next examples use separate sessions, leaving our main game
intact.

32
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:07,510
First, a two-person session is full when Joseph discovers it.

33
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:14,910
He joins the waitlist. No money is held while he waits.

34
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:21,310
With more than thirty hours left, Harrison decides to withdraw.

35
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:27,985
The app shows his full refund before he confirms.

36
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:31,700
His ten dollars returns to his wallet,

37
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:34,460
and he opens the place to the waitlist.

38
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:42,735
The next eligible player can take the opening in queue order.

39
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:51,485
Now consider a different session, starting later today.

40
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:58,560
Harrison is withdrawing late, so his share stays held.

41
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:04,535
He finds Joseph by user ID and invites him as a named
replacement.

42
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:09,860
Sending an invitation alone does not earn Harrison a refund.

43
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:22,810
Joseph must accept and cover the place before the session
starts.

44
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:31,612
Only then is Harrison refunded.

45
00:04:31,612 --> 00:04:35,210
Without a replacement, his share goes to the booker.

46
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:44,710
After tennis, Neoh closes the loop by confirming attendance.

47
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:50,310
This is a prepared ended-session example, so we can show the
next stage.

48
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:55,560
He reviews Harrison and Joseph, marks them as attended, and
saves.

49
00:04:55,600 --> 00:05:00,835
Attendance verification and withdrawing earnings are separate
actions.

50
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:05,860
Once everyone is verified, the session is ready to withdraw.

51
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:09,210
The two guest shares total twenty dollars.

52
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:14,985
This demonstration stops at readiness; it does not make a bank
transfer.

53
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:20,510
One good game gives Neoh a reason to organise another.

54
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:25,035
He creates a regular group for their Sunday tennis sessions.

55
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:30,510
He finds Harrison and Joseph by their user IDs and invites them.

56
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:36,035
An invitation is not membership. The player chooses whether to
join.

57
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:41,685
Each player accepts from their own account before becoming a
member.

58
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:52,160
Now their group is ready for the next invitation.

59
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:58,785
Neoh can organise another session with people he already knows.

60
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:03,835
Neoh started with a court, but no one to play with.

61
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:08,660
Through Booking Web Manager, he found Harrison and Joseph.

62
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:14,085
One cancelled plan became a game, and a reason to meet again.

63
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,325
Booking Web Manager

64
00:06:21,325 --> 00:06:24,835
by SC2006 Group 3.

65
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:30,300
Thank you for watching.
